projects/
state/
# data/* keeps every direct child of data/ ignored: git does not descend into an
# ignored directory, so the prevention-ledger carve-out below would never apply
# under a bare `data/` rule.
data/*
# data/ is captain-private except the prevention ledger, whose committed JSONL
# is the reviewer's comparison target for bin/fm-prevention-ledger.py. The
# ledger stores no finding description, prompt, transcript, or credential.
!data/prevention-ledger/
scratchpad*
.no-mistakes/
.lavish/
.fm-secondmate-home
.fm-secondmate-parent
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
config/

.tools/
